(The "tipster" in Wall Street is like the tout on the race track. He) Tj T*
(pretends to know all about it, and is a very solemn and mysterious) Tj T*
(individual. He tells one man to buy and another to sell, knowing that) Tj T*
(whichever way the market goes one of them will be a winner, and the) Tj T*
("tipster" will get his share. The one who wins tells his friends, who) Tj T*
(think the "tipster" must be a wonderfully shrewd individual, and in) Tj T*
(this way he builds up a profitable business, and the "lambs" come) Tj T*
(flocking his way. He keeps on telling one set of his victims to buy a) Tj T*
(certain stock, and another set to sell it. Whether the stock goes up or) Tj T*
(down the "tipster" wins, and those who are on the right side of this) Tj T*
(particular deal spread his name and fame among their acquaintances.) Tj T*
