(simply gambling, and very hazardous gambling it is. If he guesses) Tj T*
(wrong, he must pay up more and more margin or lose altogether. Dealing) Tj T*
(on margin is the favorite sport of the "lambs," and it is very) Tj T*
(profitable, indeed, to those who take advantage of their misfortunes.) Tj T*
(The odds are all against the speculator on margin, and sooner or later) Tj T*
(his money disappears and he disappears with it.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A SUCCESSFUL OPERATOR.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A man who is neither "bull" nor a "bear," but simply waits and takes) Tj T*
(advantage of opportunities. He knows the power of money. He knows the) Tj T*
(weakness of the public, and how gullible it is. He knows how to worry) Tj T*
(and scare the people. He sets his machine for the game and gets it.) Tj T*
(Ordinary market affairs do not interest him. When a "squall" appears he) Tj T*
(is notified instantly, and gets ready for business. He knows all about) Tj T*
(the stocks that he deals in, precisely what they are, and just what to) Tj T*
(do. He knows what to buy and just to a fraction when to commence to buy) Tj T*
(it. He gives his orders, pays no more attention to it, except to see) Tj T*
(how much he got. He buys just as closely to the bottom as it is) Tj T*
(possible to get, and when it is all over he goes away happy, asking to) Tj T*
ET
